WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:03.780
DC had high hopes for "Blue Beetle."&nbsp;
So why did it suffer the same fate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:08.160
as "Shazam! Fury of the Gods" and bomb big&nbsp;
time? Turns out that timing is everything.

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:12.960
Despite getting mostly positive reviews from&nbsp;
critics and audiences alike, DC's latest effort,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:16.320
"Blue Beetle," ended up flopping at the&nbsp;
box office. While "Blue Beetle" did kick&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:19.980
"Barbie" out of the top spot at the box office&nbsp;
after it spent a whopping four weeks there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:24.780
the film only earned around $25 million. So&nbsp;
what kept "Blue Beetle" from being so buzzy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:27.660
and why didn't it perform nearly&nbsp;
as well as the studio executives at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:31.380
DC and Warner Bros. likely hoped? It&nbsp;
probably came down to a few factors.

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:36.420
For one, August is a tough month to release a&nbsp;
huge movie. TV Tropes calls it a "dump month,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:39.900
and the back half of the month is usually&nbsp;
reserved for movies that aren't expected to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:43.620
perform quite as well, seeing as everybody&nbsp;
is wrapping up their summer fun. Kids are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:46.260
heading back to school or families&nbsp;
are taking one last trip together,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:49.140
so the big releases are typically&nbsp;
preserved for the holiday season.

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:53.400
There are, of course, exceptions to this rule.&nbsp;
"Guardians of the Galaxy" was released in August&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:58.140
of 2014 and became an immediate hit, and like&nbsp;
"Blue Beetle," it was also the origin story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:02.400
of comic book characters that had largely been&nbsp;
forgotten except by the most ardent of readers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:05.640
So what was the difference here? Part of&nbsp;
it comes down to the marketing campaign,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:09.600
a dearth of major movie stars, and&nbsp;
some very, very unfortunate timing.

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:13.620
"Where did you go?"
"Mama! I don't know. I think I cut a bus in half."

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:19.380
"Blue Beetle" was always a risky movie, too.&nbsp;
The film is based on a lesser-known character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:23.880
whose cast doesn't boast any enormous names,&nbsp;
with the biggest being Susan Sarandon. It's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:27.660
all frustrating because Xolo Maridueña has&nbsp;
earned praise for his central performance as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:31.740
Jaime Reyes, but while he's a fan favorite&nbsp;
on "Cobra Kai", he's not yet a huge star.

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:35.700
Marvel was able to get away with casting people&nbsp;
like Tom Hiddleston and Chris Hemsworth before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:39.180
they became two of the world's biggest stars.&nbsp;
However, for a movie to face off against&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:43.500
star-studded flicks like "Barbie," you might need&nbsp;
to pack a punch slightly bigger with the casting.

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:47.100
"Blue Beetle" also didn't wage the biggest&nbsp;
marketing campaign. To bring "Barbie" into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:50.940
it again, that movie was simply inescapable&nbsp;
this summer, while the average moviegoer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:54.360
probably wasn't even sure "Blue Beetle"&nbsp;
was coming out. There's another issue here,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:57.840
though. "Blue Beetle" simply couldn't have a&nbsp;
huge press tour to put its stars on the map,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:02.460
because of the current double strike between&nbsp;
SAG-AFTRA and the WGA against major studios.

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:06.420
In order to avoid crossing the picket line,&nbsp;
stars can't do any publicity for past,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:09.360
present, or future projects. And&nbsp;
while the stars of "Blue Beetle"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:12.600
have stood strong with SAG-AFTRA and are&nbsp;
also fighting for fair pay and treatment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:16.860
it can't be overlooked that their timing was&nbsp;
absolutely terrible when it came to publicity.

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:19.980
Frankly, DC hasn't been doing&nbsp;
themselves any favors as of late,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:23.460
either. "Shazam! Fury of the Gods" was&nbsp;
a huge flop when it came out in March,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:27.540
and despite star Zachary Levi's complaints&nbsp;
that nobody's making quality content anymore,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:31.920
that unloved movie certainly contributed to&nbsp;
superhero fatigue. As Marvel moves away from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:36.180
the one-two punch of "Avengers: Infinity War"&nbsp;
and "Endgame" and DC struggles to keep up, the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:40.320
world has gotten more and more projects that have&nbsp;
only produced diminishing returns. Things felt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:44.400
especially dire for DC when "The Flash," released&nbsp;
in the middle of June, became one of Warner Bros.'&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:48.960
biggest box office bombs. So in a way, it&nbsp;
feels like "Blue Beetle" was set up to fail.

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:52.200
"You're the Blue Beetle."
"I could use that arsenal right about now."

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:56.520
The truth is that, despite repeatedly strapping&nbsp;
on their wax wings and heading in the sun's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.520 --> 00:03:01.620
direction, DC hasn't yet reached Marvel's heights.&nbsp;
So "Blue Beetle" is another casualty, which is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:06.180
really a shame. A film that put a spotlight on&nbsp;
Latino people and introduced fresh faces into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:10.740
media landscape is a net positive, so hopefully,&nbsp;
more people will discover "Blue Beetle" with time.

